[meta]
lang: en
title: OireMark conformance tests: Footnotes
[/meta]

h1. Footnotes

Tests for Section 16 of the specification.

h2. References and Block

h3. Single footnote {#footnotes-basic}
[code om]
A claim[fn1].

[fn]
1. The source.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>A claim<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">The source. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]

h3. Repeated reference gets its own ID, back link goes to the first {#footnotes-repeated}
[code om]
Some claim[fn1] and another[fn2] and repeated[fn1].

[fn]
1. First footnote explanation.
2. Second footnote explanation.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Some claim<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup> and another<sup><a href="#fn2" id="fnref2" role="doc-noteref">2</a></sup> and repeated<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1-2" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">First footnote explanation. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
    <li id="fn2">Second footnote explanation. <a href="#fnref2" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]

h3. References may appear out of order {#footnotes-out-of-order}
[code om]
First[fn2] then[fn1].

[fn]
1. One.
2. Two.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>First<sup><a href="#fn2" id="fnref2" role="doc-noteref">2</a></sup> then<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">One. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
    <li id="fn2">Two. <a href="#fnref2" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]

h3. Definitions are output in label order {#footnotes-label-order}
[code om]
First[fn1] then[fn2].

[fn]
2. Two.
1. One.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>First<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup> then<sup><a href="#fn2" id="fnref2" role="doc-noteref">2</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">One. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
    <li id="fn2">Two. <a href="#fnref2" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]

h3. A gap in labels gets a value attribute {#footnotes-label-gap}
[code om]
First[fn1] then[fn3].

[fn]
1. One.
3. Three.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>First<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup> then<sup><a href="#fn3" id="fnref3" role="doc-noteref">3</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">One. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
    <li id="fn3" value="3">Three. <a href="#fnref3" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]

h3. Footnote IDs are reserved before heading IDs {#footnotes-id-reserved}
[code om]
h2. Fn1

A claim[fn1].

[fn]
1. The source.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<h2 id="fn1-2">Fn1</h2>
<p>A claim<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">The source. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]

h3. Blank lines between footnotes are allowed {#footnotes-blank-lines}
[code om]
First[fn1] then[fn2].

[fn]
1. One.

2. Two.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>First<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup> then<sup><a href="#fn2" id="fnref2" role="doc-noteref">2</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">One. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
    <li id="fn2">Two. <a href="#fnref2" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]

h3. A line that is not "N. text" is an error {#footnotes-invalid-line}
[code om]
A claim[fn1].

[fn]
1. The source.
More about the source.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-nesting 5
[/code]

h3. A # marker in the footnote block is an error {#footnotes-hash-marker}
[code om]
A claim[fn1].

[fn]
# The source.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-nesting 4
[/code]

h3. Footnote content with formatting and a link {#footnotes-formatted-content}
[code om]
Details[fn1].

[fn]
1. See the *official documentation* at [example.com]:https://example.com for details.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Details<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">See the <strong>official documentation</strong> at <a href="https://example.com">example.com</a> for details. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]

h3. Footnote content with code and emphasis {#footnotes-code-content}
[code om]
Details[fn1].

[fn]
1. This includes `code samples` and _emphasized text_.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Details<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">This includes <code>code samples</code> and <em>emphasized text</em>. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]

h2. Back Link

h3. Configured back-link symbol {#footnotes-backlink-option}
; backlink
: ↑
[code om]
A claim[fn1].

[fn]
1. The source.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>A claim<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">The source. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↑</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]

h2. Problems That Are Warnings

h3. Reference without a definition renders literally {#footnotes-undefined}
[code om]
Claim[fn1] and[fn2].

[fn]
1. Source.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Claim<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup> and[fn2].</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">Source. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]
[code warnings]
footnote-undefined 1
[/code]

h3. Reference with no footnote block at all {#footnotes-undefined-no-block}
[code om]
A claim[fn1].
[/code]
[code html]
<p>A claim[fn1].</p>
[/code]
[code warnings]
footnote-undefined 1
[/code]

h3. Unused definition renders without a back link {#footnotes-unused}
[code om]
A claim[fn1].

[fn]
1. The source.
2. Never cited.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>A claim<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">The source. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
    <li id="fn2">Never cited.</li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]
[code warnings]
footnote-unused 5
[/code]

h3. Duplicate definition: the last one wins {#footnotes-duplicate}
[code om]
Claim[fn1].

[fn]
1. Old text.
1. New text.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Claim<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">New text. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]
[code warnings]
footnote-duplicate 5
[/code]

h2. Placement

h3. A comment may follow the footnote block {#footnotes-comment-after}
[code om]
A claim[fn1].

[fn]
1. The source.
[/fn]

[comment]
Reviewed.
[/comment]
[/code]
[code html]
<p>A claim<sup><a href="#fn1" id="fnref1" role="doc-noteref">1</a></sup>.</p>
<section class="footnotes" role="doc-endnotes">
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">The source. <a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩</a></li>
  </ol>
</section>
[/code]

h3. Content after the footnote block is an error {#footnotes-content-after}
[code om]
A claim[fn1].

[fn]
1. The source.
[/fn]

More text.
[/code]
[code error]
footnote-block-misplaced 7
[/code]

h3. A second footnote block is an error {#footnotes-second-block}
[code om]
A claim[fn1] and another[fn2].

[fn]
1. The source.
[/fn]

[fn]
2. Another source.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code error]
footnote-block-misplaced 7
[/code]

h2. Profiles

h3. A reference is an error in the standard profile {#footnotes-profile-standard-reference}
; profile
: standard
[code om]
Intro.

A claim[fn1].
[/code]
[code error]
feature-not-in-profile 3
[/code]

h3. Footnotes are not allowed in the standard profile {#footnotes-profile-standard}
; profile
: standard
[code om]
[fn]
1. The source.
[/fn]
[/code]
[code error]
feature-not-in-profile 1
[/code]
